  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $\u2016u\u2016=15$ and $\u2016u+\\sqrt{5}v\u2016=75.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $\u2016v\u2016.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $u$ is orthogonal to $\\sqrt{5}v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016u+\\sqrt{5}v{\u2016}^{2} & =\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}+\u2016\\sqrt{5}v{\u2016}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016u+\\sqrt{5}v{\u2016}^{2} & =\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}+(\\sqrt{5}\u2016v\u2016)^{2} \\\\ \u2016u+\\sqrt{5}v{\u2016}^{2} & =\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}+5\u2016v{\u2016}^{2} \\\\ (75)^{2} & =(15)^{2}+5\u2016v{\u2016}^{2} \\\\ 5\\,625 & =225+5\u2016v{\u2016}^{2} \\\\ 5\\,400 & =5\u2016v{\u2016}^{2} \\\\ \u2016v{\u2016}^{2} & =1\\,080\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\u2016v\u2016=6\\sqrt{30}.$",
